-include: ../../../bundle-parent/annotations.bnd
Import-Package: ${annotation-noimports}, *
Bundle-SymbolicName: io.seedmatic.rke2lab.manifests.ingress
Export-Package: io.seedmatic.rke2lab.manifests.ingress
# type=dual-realm — the manifests domain's dual-realm host face: the version pins BOTH realms
# genuinely consume. ComponentVersions is the single source of truth for the bootstrap-layer
# component versions: OSGi-side the manifest units read it through the synthesis context; host-side
# the manifests-cli `versions` bumper reads ComponentVersions.defaults() FLAT to diff each pin
# against its upstream GitHub release. Like seed-broker-codec it is staged as a bundle OSGi-side AND
# kept flat host-side, so its exported package legitimately lives in two realms and
# DUPLICATE_REALM_CLASS exempts it. NOT a seam surface between DOMAINS: producer (the manifests
# units) and consumer (the manifests bumper) are the SAME domain — orthogonal to the contract-purity
# guard.
#
# GOVERNANCE (the dual-realm library rule): the red line is NOT "no logic" — it is "no dependency
# absent from either realm". A type may carry pure logic here IFF it depends only on the JDK +
# jspecify (no OSGi type, no other domain, no service reference) and is owned by this one domain.
# REALM_BOUNDARY reads method bodies via ASM and breaks the build on any forbidden reference, so this
# is machine-enforced. ComponentVersions qualifies: a pure String value record with a builder, zero
# imports, manifests-owned, consumed on both sides. It carries no @Component, so it does NOT Require
# the SCR extender.
Provide-Capability: io.seedmatic.rke2lab.embed; type=dual-realm
